# BuildKit reads this file for `-f production/mobile-moba/server/Dockerfile`, so the exclusions stay scoped
# to the match-server image instead of becoming a repository-wide .dockerignore that surprises other builds.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs `gameplay/`, `match-server/`, and one manifest, but the daemon still receives the
# whole context first. This repository carries multi-hundred-megabyte CAD fixtures, a renderer, an editor
# front end, and huge build outputs; without these exclusions the context transfer dominates the build.
#
# Deny everything, then re-include the exact three paths. A nested re-include needs its whole parent chain
# spelled out — excluding `production/` outright would stop the walk before it can reach the manifest — so
# each level is re-included and then narrowed again.

*

!gameplay
!match-server

!production
production/*
!production/mobile-moba
production/mobile-moba/*
!production/mobile-moba/server
production/mobile-moba/server/*
!production/mobile-moba/server/container-workspace.toml

# Build outputs inside the re-included crates. These come last so they win over the re-includes above.
gameplay/target
match-server/target
**/*.rs.bk
